# ─── Storefront proxy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drop product pages are server-rendered by the ARK app on Railway, but they must
# be SERVED from this apex domain, because that is where the site's search
# authority lives. Every drop page's canonical tag already says
# arkscreenprinting.com/shop/<slug>; these two rules are what make that URL real.
#
# Status 200 makes it a REWRITE, not a redirect: the visitor and Googlebot both
# see the apex URL in the address bar and never learn the app subdomain exists.
# A 301 here would hand the authority straight back to the subdomain and defeat
# the point.
#
# The trailing "!" is force, which makes these win over any static file that might
# later be added at /shop. Nothing shadows them today.
#
# Both lines are needed: "/shop/*" does not reliably match the bare "/shop", and
# bare /shop is the storefront hub — the only URL in the drop sitemap and the
# target of every drop page's breadcrumb.
#
# ⚠️ ?arkSurface=apex is LOAD-BEARING — do not drop it when editing these rules.
#
# The app must know it is being served at the apex, because it withholds pages
# from the index when it believes it is answering on the app subdomain. It used
# to infer that from X-Forwarded-Host. That was measured against this very proxy
# and it does not work: with the rewrite live and no marker, the apex answered
#
#     X-Ark-Surface: app     X-Robots-Tag: noindex
#
# — i.e. every product page at the apex would have been withheld from Google,
# silently, with nothing visibly wrong in the HTML. Netlify's status-200 proxy
# does not deliver a usable X-Forwarded-Host here.
#
# So the proxy tags its own requests instead. The app checks this marker first
# and strips it from any redirect, so it never reaches a visitor's address bar.
# Verify after any change to this file:
#
#     curl -sI https://arkscreenprinting.com/shop | grep -i x-ark-surface
#     → apex  correct.   → app  STOP, pages will not be indexed.
#
# Rollback: delete this file. The pages keep working on the subdomain.

/shop      https://design.arkscreenprinting.com/shop?arkSurface=apex         200!
/shop/*    https://design.arkscreenprinting.com/shop/:splat?arkSurface=apex   200!
